WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.750
Heat iron ore with carbon in
a furnace, and out comes iron.

2
00:00:04.800 --> 00:00:07.690
Carbon pulls the oxygen
away from the metal.

3
00:00:07.740 --> 00:00:10.650
Now try the same trick
with aluminium oxide.

4
00:00:10.700 --> 00:00:13.130
Same carbon, same kind of furnace.

5
00:00:13.180 --> 00:00:15.150
No aluminium comes out.

6
00:00:15.200 --> 00:00:20.110
Yet aluminium is all around
us, in cans, foil and aircraft.

7
00:00:20.160 --> 00:00:24.130
So why does carbon work for
iron, but not for aluminium?

8
00:00:24.180 --> 00:00:27.690
In this mission, you'll meet
the reactivity series and find

9
00:00:27.740 --> 00:00:29.530
where carbon fits into it.

10
00:00:29.580 --> 00:00:33.370
You'll see how carbon can take
oxygen from a metal oxide,

11
00:00:33.420 --> 00:00:36.790
and how a metal's place in the
series decides how we get it out

12
00:00:36.840 --> 00:00:38.150
of the ground.

13
00:00:38.200 --> 00:00:43.300
Your mission: explain why carbon
frees iron but not aluminium.
